.TH WARD 1 "October 2026" "Ward v1.0.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ward \- private messaging on the open XMPP network
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ward
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIURI\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ward
is an XMPP (Jabber) client for GTK 4 and libadwaita. Chats are end-to-end encrypted with OMEMO by default;
OpenPGP is available as an option and shares its keys with GPGMan and GnuPG.
.PP
Running
.B ward
while it is already running brings the existing window to the front. xmpp: links (RFC 5122) given on the
command line open the right chat, group or invitation.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-background
Start without a window and stay connected; used by "Start at login".
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quit
Quit the running instance.
.TP
.B \-\-check
Print which libraries and optional features are available, with the commands to install what is missing,
and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Log everything to the terminal. Passwords and tokens are masked.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a short help.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B WARD_HOME
Keep all settings, history and caches in this folder instead of the XDG folders.
.TP
.B WARD_LOG
Log level: debug, info or warning.
.TP
.B WARD_OFFLINE
When set, open everything without connecting.
.TP
.B WARD_SECRETS
Where passwords are kept: keyring, file or memory (overrides the per-account setting).
.TP
.B WARD_VENDOR
An extra folder of Python libraries (set by the launcher that install.sh writes).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/ward/settings.json
Settings. Accounts and per-chat settings are in the database.
.TP
.I ~/.config/ward/custom.css
Optional style sheet, loaded last when enabled in Preferences.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/ward/ward.db
Messages, contacts, chats and encryption keys (SQLite).
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/ward/python
Libraries Ward installed itself (encryption support).
.TP
.I ~/.cache/ward
Downloaded files, thumbnails and avatars.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B ward xmpp:alex@example.org?message
Open a chat with alex@example.org.
.TP
.B ward \-\-check
See what is missing on this machine.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR gpg (1),
.BR prosody (1)
.PP
https://github.com/smiley-mcsmiles/ward
